  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '1.12', 'Numerical Methods', 'What does the change of sign method rely on?', 'If f is continuous on [a, b] and f(a) and f(b) have opposite signs, there is a root between a and b.', 1),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '1.12', 'Numerical Methods', 'Why can a change of sign occur without a root?', 'At a vertical asymptote (discontinuity), e.g. f(x) = 1/x between −1 and 1.', 2),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '1.12', 'Numerical Methods', 'Why might there be a root with no change of sign?', 'A repeated root where the curve touches the x-axis, or two roots close together.', 3),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '1.12', 'Numerical Methods', 'What is decimal search?', 'Checking values at intervals of 0.1, then 0.01, etc., to locate a root by change of sign.', 4),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '1.12', 'Numerical Methods', 'What is interval bisection?', 'Repeatedly halving the interval containing the root and keeping the half with a sign change.', 5),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '1.12', 'Numerical Methods', 'How do you rearrange f(x) = 0 into x = g(x)?', 'Make x the subject of part of the equation, e.g. x³ − x − 1 = 0 → x = ∛(x + 1).', 6),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '1.12', 'Numerical Methods', 'What is the convergence condition for xₙ₊₁ = g(xₙ)?', '|g′(x)| < 1 near the root.', 7),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '1.12', 'Numerical Methods', 'What is a staircase diagram?', 'A diagram showing iteration converging monotonically, when 0 < g′(x) < 1.', 8),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '1.12', 'Numerical Methods', 'What is a cobweb diagram?', 'A diagram showing iteration oscillating around the root, when −1 < g′(x) < 0.', 9),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '1.12', 'Numerical Methods', 'Apply one step of Newton–Raphson to f(x) = x² − 2 from x₀ = 1.', 'x₁ = 1 − (1 − 2)/2 = 1.5.', 10),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '1.12', 'Numerical Methods', 'When does the trapezium rule give an overestimate?', 'When the curve is concave up (convex) over the interval.', 11),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '1.12', 'Numerical Methods', 'When does the trapezium rule give an underestimate?', 'When the curve is concave down over the interval.', 12),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '1.12', 'Numerical Methods', 'How do you improve the accuracy of the trapezium rule?', 'Increase the number of strips (decrease the strip width).', 13),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '1.12', 'Numerical Methods', 'What is the width h in the trapezium rule?', 'h = (b − a)/n, where n is the number of strips.', 14),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '1.13', 'Vectors', 'What is the zero vector?', 'A vector with zero magnitude and no specific direction.', 1),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '1.13', 'Vectors', 'Find the magnitude of 3i − 4j.', '√(9 + 16) = 5.', 2),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '1.13', 'Vectors', 'Find the unit vector in the direction of 3i − 4j.', '(3i − 4j)/5 = 0.6i − 0.8j.', 3),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '1.13', 'Vectors', 'If a = 2i + j and b = i − 3j, find 2a − b.', '4i + 2j − i + 3j = 3i + 5j.', 4),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '1.13', 'Vectors', 'What is a position vector?', 'A vector giving the position of a point relative to the origin.', 5),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '1.13', 'Vectors', 'Find the direction of 3i + 3j.', '45° above the positive x-axis.', 6),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '1.13', 'Vectors', 'What is the magnitude of 2i − j + 2k?', '√(4 + 1 + 4) = 3.', 7),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '1.13', 'Vectors', 'How do you find a vector of magnitude 10 in the direction of 3i + 4j?', 'Unit vector (3i + 4j)/5, times 10: 6i + 8j.', 8),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '1.13', 'Vectors', 'If AB = b − a, what is BA?', 'a − b.', 9),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '1.13', 'Vectors', 'What is the resultant of forces (3i + 2j) N and (−i + 4j) N?', '2i + 6j N.', 10),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '1.13', 'Vectors', 'Express 10 N at 30° above the x-axis in component form.', '10 cos 30° i + 10 sin 30° j = 5√3 i + 5j N.', 11),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '1.13', 'Vectors', 'How do you show two vectors are parallel?', 'Show one is a scalar multiple of the other.', 12),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '1.13', 'Vectors', 'What is a column vector?', 'A vector written vertically with components, e.g. (3, 4) written as a column.', 13),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '1.13', 'Vectors', 'What does it mean for vectors to be equal?', 'They have the same magnitude and direction (equal components).', 14),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.1', 'Sampling', 'What is a census?', 'Data collected from every member of the population.', 1),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.1', 'Sampling', 'What are the advantages of a census?', 'It is complete and accurate, with no sampling variability.', 2),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.1', 'Sampling', 'What are the disadvantages of a census?', 'It is expensive and time-consuming, and impractical for large populations or destructive tests.', 3),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.1', 'Sampling', 'What are the advantages of sampling?', 'Cheaper, quicker and more practical than a census.', 4),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.1', 'Sampling', 'What is a representative sample?', 'A sample that reflects the characteristics of the population.', 5),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.1', 'Sampling', 'How is a simple random sample selected?', 'Number each member of the sampling frame and use random numbers to select them.', 6),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.1', 'Sampling', 'What is the advantage of stratified sampling?', 'It ensures each subgroup is represented in proportion to its size.', 7),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.1', 'Sampling', 'What is the disadvantage of quota sampling?', 'It is non-random, so interviewer bias may occur.', 8),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.1', 'Sampling', 'What is the advantage of systematic sampling?', 'It is simple and quick to carry out.', 9),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.1', 'Sampling', 'What is the disadvantage of cluster sampling?', 'Clusters may not be representative of the whole population.', 10),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.1', 'Sampling', 'What is the advantage of opportunity sampling?', 'It is quick, easy and cheap.', 11),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.1', 'Sampling', 'What is non-response bias?', 'Bias caused when people who don''t respond differ from those who do.', 12),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.1', 'Sampling', 'What is the population in a statistical study?', 'The whole group of interest.', 13),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.1', 'Sampling', 'What is sampling variability?', 'Different samples from the same population give different results.', 14),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.2', 'Data Presentation & Interpretation', 'What is discrete data?', 'Data that can only take specific values, often counts, e.g. the number of goals.', 1),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.2', 'Data Presentation & Interpretation', 'What is continuous data?', 'Data that can take any value in a range, e.g. height or time.', 2),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.2', 'Data Presentation & Interpretation', 'What is categorical data?', 'Data in categories, e.g. colour or type.', 3),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.2', 'Data Presentation & Interpretation', 'What is ranked data?', 'Ordinal data that can be put in order.', 4),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.2', 'Data Presentation & Interpretation', 'What is frequency density?', 'Frequency ÷ class width, used for histogram heights.', 5),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.2', 'Data Presentation & Interpretation', 'What is the interquartile range?', 'Upper quartile − lower quartile, the range of the middle 50%.', 6),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.2', 'Data Presentation & Interpretation', 'What is the mode?', 'The most frequent value.', 7),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.2', 'Data Presentation & Interpretation', 'What is the midrange?', '(Maximum + minimum) ÷ 2.', 8),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.2', 'Data Presentation & Interpretation', 'How is the mean calculated from a frequency table?', 'Σfx ÷ Σf.', 9),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.2', 'Data Presentation & Interpretation', 'What is the root mean square deviation?', '√(Sxx/n), where Sxx = Σ(x − x̄)².', 10),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.2', 'Data Presentation & Interpretation', 'What is Sxx?', 'Σ(x − x̄)² = Σx² − (Σx)²/n.', 11),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.2', 'Data Presentation & Interpretation', 'What does positive skew look like?', 'A long tail to the right; mean > median > mode.', 12),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.2', 'Data Presentation & Interpretation', 'What does negative skew look like?', 'A long tail to the left; mean < median < mode.', 13),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.2', 'Data Presentation & Interpretation', 'What does a scatter diagram show?', 'The relationship between two variables for bivariate data.', 14),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.3', 'Probability', 'What is a sample space?', 'The set of all possible outcomes.', 1),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.3', 'Probability', 'What is an event?', 'A set of outcomes from the sample space.', 2),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.3', 'Probability', 'What is P(A'') ?', '1 − P(A), the probability that A doesn''t happen.', 3),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.3', 'Probability', 'If P(A) = 0.4 and P(B) = 0.5 and A and B are independent, find P(A ∩ B).', '0.4 × 0.5 = 0.2.', 4),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.3', 'Probability', 'If A and B are mutually exclusive, what is P(A ∪ B)?', 'P(A) + P(B).', 5),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.3', 'Probability', 'What is P(A ∪ B) in general?', 'P(A) + P(B) − P(A ∩ B).', 6),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.3', 'Probability', 'What is P(A | B)?', 'P(A ∩ B)/P(B).', 7),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.3', 'Probability', 'What is a two-way table used for?', 'Showing frequencies for two categorical variables, useful for finding conditional probabilities.', 8),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.3', 'Probability', 'How do you find the probability of at least one success?', '1 − P(no successes).', 9),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.3', 'Probability', 'How many ways can 5 people be arranged in a line?', '5! = 120.', 10),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.3', 'Probability', 'How many ways can 3 people be chosen from 8?', '⁸C₃ = 56.', 11),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.3', 'Probability', 'What is P(A | A)?', '1.', 12),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.3', 'Probability', 'What does it mean if P(A | B) = P(A)?', 'A and B are independent.', 13),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.3', 'Probability', 'What is the probability of two sixes when rolling two fair dice?', '1/6 × 1/6 = 1/36.', 14),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.4', 'Probability Distributions', 'What is the probability function of a random variable?', 'A rule giving P(X = x) for each value x.', 1),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.4', 'Probability Distributions', 'What is E(X) for a discrete random variable?', 'Σ x P(X = x).', 2),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.4', 'Probability Distributions', 'What is the probability of rolling a 4 on a fair die (discrete uniform)?', '1/6.', 3),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.4', 'Probability Distributions', 'Find P(X = 2) if X ~ B(5, 0.3).', '⁵C₂ × 0.3² × 0.7³ = 10 × 0.09 × 0.343 = 0.3087.', 4),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.4', 'Probability Distributions', 'What is the variance of a binomial distribution?', 'np(1 − p).', 5),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.4', 'Probability Distributions', 'What is the shape of a binomial distribution when p = 0.5?', 'Symmetrical.', 6),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.4', 'Probability Distributions', 'What is the shape of a binomial distribution when p < 0.5?', 'Positively skewed.', 7),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.4', 'Probability Distributions', 'How do you find P(X ≤ 3) using a calculator?', 'Use the binomial cumulative distribution function.', 8),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.4', 'Probability Distributions', 'What is the probability of a single value for a continuous distribution?', 'Zero; probabilities are only found for intervals.', 9),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.4', 'Probability Distributions', 'What is the mean and variance of Z ~ N(0, 1)?', 'Mean 0 and variance 1.', 10),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.4', 'Probability Distributions', 'If X ~ N(50, 16), find P(X < 54).', 'Z = (54 − 50)/4 = 1: P(Z < 1) ≈ 0.8413.', 11),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.4', 'Probability Distributions', 'What is the inverse Normal used for?', 'To find the value of x corresponding to a given probability.', 12),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.4', 'Probability Distributions', 'When can a binomial B(n, p) be approximated by a Normal?', 'When n is large and p is close to 0.5 (np and n(1 − p) both greater than about 5).', 13),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.4', 'Probability Distributions', 'What Normal approximation is used for B(n, p)?', 'N(np, np(1 − p)).', 14),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.5', 'Statistical Hypothesis Testing', 'What is a test statistic?', 'A value calculated from sample data used to decide whether to reject H₀.', 1),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.5', 'Statistical Hypothesis Testing', 'What is a Type I error?', 'Rejecting H₀ when it is true.', 2),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.5', 'Statistical Hypothesis Testing', 'What is the probability of a Type I error?', 'The actual significance level (the probability of the observed value being in the critical region if H₀ is true).', 3),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.5', 'Statistical Hypothesis Testing', 'State the hypotheses for testing whether a coin is biased towards heads.', 'H₀: p = 0.5; H₁: p > 0.5, where p is the probability of heads.', 4),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.5', 'Statistical Hypothesis Testing', 'What does a significance level of 5% mean?', 'The probability of rejecting H₀ when it is true is at most 5%.', 5),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.5', 'Statistical Hypothesis Testing', 'What is the conclusion if the p-value is less than the significance level?', 'Reject H₀: there is sufficient evidence to support H₁.', 6),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.5', 'Statistical Hypothesis Testing', 'What is the conclusion if the test statistic isn''t in the critical region?', 'Do not reject H₀: there is insufficient evidence to support H₁.', 7),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.5', 'Statistical Hypothesis Testing', 'How do you find a critical region for a binomial test?', 'Find the values where the cumulative probability in the tail is less than or equal to the significance level.', 8),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.5', 'Statistical Hypothesis Testing', 'What is the sampling distribution of the mean for a Normal population?', 'X̄ ~ N(μ, σ²/n).', 9),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.5', 'Statistical Hypothesis Testing', 'What is the test statistic for a Normal mean test?', 'z = (x̄ − μ)/(σ/√n).', 10),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.5', 'Statistical Hypothesis Testing', 'What is the critical value for a one-tailed 5% Normal test?', '1.645.', 11),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.5', 'Statistical Hypothesis Testing', 'What is the critical value for a two-tailed 5% Normal test?', '±1.96.', 12),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.5', 'Statistical Hypothesis Testing', 'Why should conclusions be stated in context?', 'The conclusion must relate to the original problem, not just state "reject H₀".', 13),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '2.5', 'Statistical Hypothesis Testing', 'What is a hypothesis test on a correlation coefficient used for?', 'To test whether there is evidence of correlation in the population, using the sample correlation coefficient.', 14),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.1', 'Models & Quantities', 'What is a mathematical model?', 'A simplified representation of a real-world situation using mathematics.', 1),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.1', 'Models & Quantities', 'What is a modelling assumption?', 'A simplification made to make a model easier to use, e.g. ignoring air resistance.', 2),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.1', 'Models & Quantities', 'Why do we ignore air resistance in many models?', 'It simplifies calculations; the effect may be small for dense, slow objects.', 3),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.1', 'Models & Quantities', 'What does modelling an object as a lamina mean?', 'Treating it as two-dimensional with negligible thickness.', 4),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.1', 'Models & Quantities', 'What does modelling a surface as rough mean?', 'Friction acts between the surface and an object in contact with it.', 5),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.1', 'Models & Quantities', 'What does modelling a rope as a light string mean?', 'Its mass is negligible, so tension is the same throughout.', 6),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.1', 'Models & Quantities', 'What is a peg?', 'A fixed support, usually modelled as smooth, over which a string can pass.', 7),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.1', 'Models & Quantities', 'What is a bead?', 'A particle with a hole threaded on a wire or string.', 8),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.1', 'Models & Quantities', 'What is a rod?', 'A long, thin rigid body, usually modelled as having negligible thickness.', 9),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.1', 'Models & Quantities', 'What is the unit of mass?', 'Kilogram (kg).', 10),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.1', 'Models & Quantities', 'What is the unit of force?', 'Newton (N).', 11),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.1', 'Models & Quantities', 'What is the unit of acceleration?', 'Metres per second squared (m s⁻²).', 12),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.1', 'Models & Quantities', 'How do you convert 72 km h⁻¹ to m s⁻¹?', '72 × 1000 ÷ 3600 = 20 m s⁻¹.', 13),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.1', 'Models & Quantities', 'What is weight?', 'The force due to gravity on an object: W = mg.', 14),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.2', 'Kinematics in 1 Dimension', 'What is acceleration?', 'The rate of change of velocity.', 1),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.2', 'Kinematics in 1 Dimension', 'What does a horizontal line on a velocity–time graph show?', 'Constant velocity (zero acceleration).', 2),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.2', 'Kinematics in 1 Dimension', 'What does a straight line with positive gradient on a velocity–time graph show?', 'Constant acceleration.', 3),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.2', 'Kinematics in 1 Dimension', 'What does a horizontal line on a displacement–time graph show?', 'The object is stationary.', 4),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.2', 'Kinematics in 1 Dimension', 'A car decelerates from 20 m s⁻¹ to rest in 5 s. What is its acceleration?', 'a = (0 − 20)/5 = −4 m s⁻².', 5),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.2', 'Kinematics in 1 Dimension', 'A ball is dropped from 20 m. How long does it take to hit the ground (g = 9.8)?', 's = ½gt²: 20 = 4.9t², t ≈ 2.02 s.', 6),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.2', 'Kinematics in 1 Dimension', 'What is the acceleration of an object in free fall?', 'g ≈ 9.8 m s⁻² downwards (ignoring air resistance).', 7),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.2', 'Kinematics in 1 Dimension', 'Which suvat equation doesn''t include time?', 'v² = u² + 2as.', 8),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.2', 'Kinematics in 1 Dimension', 'Which suvat equation doesn''t include final velocity?', 's = ut + ½at².', 9),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.2', 'Kinematics in 1 Dimension', 'Which suvat equation doesn''t include acceleration?', 's = ½(u + v)t.', 10),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.2', 'Kinematics in 1 Dimension', 'If v = 3t² − 2t, find the acceleration at t = 2.', 'a = dv/dt = 6t − 2 = 10 m s⁻².', 11),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.2', 'Kinematics in 1 Dimension', 'If a = 6t and v = 0 at t = 0, find v.', 'v = ∫6t dt = 3t² + c; c = 0, so v = 3t².', 12),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.2', 'Kinematics in 1 Dimension', 'What does a curved displacement–time graph show?', 'The velocity is changing (acceleration).', 13),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.2', 'Kinematics in 1 Dimension', 'How is the distance found from a velocity–time graph with negative sections?', 'Add the magnitudes of the areas above and below the axis.', 14),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.3', 'Kinematics in 2 Dimensions', 'What is a velocity vector?', 'A vector giving the speed and direction of motion.', 1),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.3', 'Kinematics in 2 Dimensions', 'If r = (2t + 1)i + (t² − 3)j, find the velocity at t = 1.', 'v = 2i + 2tj; at t = 1, v = 2i + 2j.', 2),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.3', 'Kinematics in 2 Dimensions', 'How do you find the direction of motion from a velocity vector?', 'Use the angle θ = arctan(vᵧ/vₓ), taking care with the quadrant.', 3),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.3', 'Kinematics in 2 Dimensions', 'When is a particle moving parallel to the i-direction?', 'When the j-component of velocity is zero.', 4),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.3', 'Kinematics in 2 Dimensions', 'How do you find the position vector from a velocity vector?', 'Integrate each component with respect to time and add a vector constant.', 5),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.3', 'Kinematics in 2 Dimensions', 'If a = 2i − j, u = 3i + j, find v at t = 2.', 'v = u + at = 3i + j + 4i − 2j = 7i − j.', 6),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.3', 'Kinematics in 2 Dimensions', 'Find the displacement using s = ut + ½at² with u = i, a = 2j, t = 3.', 's = 3i + ½ × 2j × 9 = 3i + 9j.', 7),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.3', 'Kinematics in 2 Dimensions', 'What does r = r₀ + vt describe?', 'The position of a particle moving with constant velocity v from position r₀.', 8),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.3', 'Kinematics in 2 Dimensions', 'What is relative velocity in 2D?', 'The velocity of one object as seen from another: v_A − v_B.', 9),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.3', 'Kinematics in 2 Dimensions', 'When is a particle at the origin?', 'When both components of its position vector are zero at the same time.', 10),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.3', 'Kinematics in 2 Dimensions', 'How do you find the time when a particle is due north of the origin?', 'Set the i-component (east) of the position vector to zero, with the j-component positive.', 11),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.3', 'Kinematics in 2 Dimensions', 'How do you find the speed at time t?', 'Find the magnitude of the velocity vector.', 12),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.3', 'Kinematics in 2 Dimensions', 'How do you show that acceleration is constant?', 'Show that the acceleration vector doesn''t depend on t.', 13),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.3', 'Kinematics in 2 Dimensions', 'What is the distance between two particles at time t?', 'The magnitude of the difference between their position vectors.', 14),
  ('Mathematics', 'OCR B', 'alevel', '3.4', 'Projectiles', 'What is a projectile?', 'An object projected into the air that moves under gravity alone (in the simple model).', 1),
